      "math_academy_id": "e-5133",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\dfrac {(n + 1)(n + 3)} {4n^2} \\cdot \\dfrac {8n}{(n + 3)(n - 2)}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we cancel any terms that appear in both a numerator and a denominator. Then, we multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n+1)(n+3)}{4{n}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{8n}{(n+3)(n-2)} & =\\frac{(n+1)\\cancel{(n+3)}}{\\cancel{4n}\\cdot n}\\cdot \\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{4n}}{\\cancel{(n+3)}(n-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{n+1}{n}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2n+2}{{n}^{2}-2n}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
